  "question": {
    "text": "One Faraday of electricity liberates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> gram atom of copper from copper sulphate, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>One Faraday of electricity means it is equivalent to one mole of electrons charge.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>–</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>Cu</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> Faraday <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><mi>Cu</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> Faraday <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo><mi>Cu</mi></math> deposit</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo> </mo><mi>atom</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
